response:
To implement a depth-first traversal of a binary tree, you can use recursion or iteration.

Recursive approach:
```
void dfs(Node* node) {
    if (node == NULL) return;
    // process the current node
    dfs(node->left);
    dfs(node->right);
}
```

Iterative approach using a stack:
```
void dfs(Node* node) {
    Stack<Node*> stack;
    while (!stack.isEmpty() || node != NULL) {
        if (node == NULL) {
            node = stack.pop();
        } else {
            // process the current node
            stack.push(node->right);
            node = node->left;
        }
    }
}
```

In both approaches, you start at the root of the tree and then recursively or iteratively visit each node's left subtree, then its right subtree.

